---
/**
 * About page
 */
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PhoneLink from '../components/ui/PhoneLink.astro';
import WhatsAppCTA from '../components/ui/WhatsAppCTA';
import { siteConfig } from '../config/site';

const { name, phone } = siteConfig;
---

<BaseLayout title="About Heritage Joiners | Time-Served Bench Hand Joiner & Site Carpenter, Pontefract" description="Heritage Joiners is led by a fully qualified, time served, bench hand joiner and site carpenter — 35+ years on listed and period timber across Yorkshire.">
  <section class="py-16 lg:py-24 bg-paper">
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="max-w-3xl">
        <p class="text-oak uppercase tracking-wide mb-4">{name}</p>
        <h1 class="font-display text-4xl lg:text-5xl text-ink mb-8">
          About Heritage Joiners
        </h1>
        <div class="prose prose-lg text-ink">
          <p>
            Heritage Joiners is led by Rob — a fully qualified, time served, bench hand joiner and site carpenter with more than 35 years of hands-on experience across new builds, refurbishments, and specialist heritage work.
          </p>
          <p>
            The background covers workshop bench joinery — hand cutting, profiling, traditional jointing — through to site carpentry on new-build and commercial work, then progressively into the repair and restoration of listed and period buildings. Oak-framed buildings, barn conversions, listed commercial properties, period houses. That progression matters: it means the structural, the joinery, and the finishing judgement all come from the same hands.
          </p>
          <p>
            I work this way because original timber in a period building deserves a proper assessment before anyone talks about ripping it out. A lot of period windows, doors, frames, structural beams, and floor joists can be repaired soundly with the right judgement, timber selection, and splice work. Most are not beyond saving. Some are — and where they are, I will say so clearly.
          </p>
          <p>
            That is not repair-at-any-cost. It is repair where it is the right answer, and honest replacement where it is not.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-16 bg-bone">
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-2 gap-12">
      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl lg:text-3xl text-ink mb-4">Why repair-first</h2>
        <p class="text-ink/70">
          Listed and period buildings are strongest when the original fabric is respected. Repair can often preserve character, reduce disruption, avoid unnecessary consent routes, and keep the building's historic detail intact.
        </p>
        <a href="/repair-or-replace" class="inline-block mt-6 text-oak font-display">Read the four-stage framework &rarr;</a>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl lg:text-3xl text-ink mb-4">Where we work</h2>
        <p class="text-ink/70">
          Based in Pontefract. We work on listed and period properties across West Yorkshire — Pontefract, Wakefield, Castleford, Featherstone, Knottingley, Normanton — and travel further across Yorkshire for Leeds, York, and selected heritage projects.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-16 bg-white">
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl lg:text-3xl text-ink mb-8">Approach to listed and period work</h2>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
        <div class="p-6 bg-paper rounded-lg border border-ink/10">
          <h3 class="font-display text-xl text-ink mb-3">Assess first</h3>
          <p class="text-ink/70">Decay depth, sound timber percentage, joint condition, and previous repairs all shape the recommendation.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="p-6 bg-paper rounded-lg border border-ink/10">
          <h3 class="font-display text-xl text-ink mb-3">Match carefully</h3>
          <p class="text-ink/70">Where new timber is needed, the aim is sympathetic repair, profile retention, and a finish that settles into the building.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="p-6 bg-paper rounded-lg border border-ink/10">
          <h3 class="font-display text-xl text-ink mb-3">Keep it honest</h3>
          <p class="text-ink/70">Some timber should be retained, some sections should be replaced, and sometimes a full replacement is the correct answer.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-16 bg-bone">
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-2 gap-12">
      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl lg:text-3xl text-ink mb-4">Notable project</h2>
        <p class="text-ink/70 mb-6">
          The Counting House in Pontefract is the current anchor case study for the site, covering period timber restoration across windows, doors, and timber matching.
        </p>
        <a href="/case-studies/counting-house" class="text-oak font-display">View Counting House &rarr;</a>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl lg:text-3xl text-ink mb-4">What we do not do</h2>
        <p class="text-ink/70 mb-3">
          Heritage Joiners is a specialist business, not a general joinery contractor. We do not take on kitchens, decking, painting-as-the-main-service, general domestic joinery, or handyman work.
        </p>
        <p class="text-ink/70">
          The work we take on: listed building timber repair (Grade I, Grade II*, Grade II), period property repair and restoration, conservation area properties, structural timber programmes (beams, joists, roof timbers, frames), heritage interior joinery (panelling, floors), and whole-property programmes for owners doing comprehensive restoration.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-16 bg-ink text-bone">
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 text-center">
      <h2 class="font-display text-3xl mb-4">Get in touch</h2>
      <p class="text-bone/70 mb-8 mx-auto">
        Send photos first and Rob can usually give an initial view on whether repair looks viable.
      </p>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-4">
        <WhatsAppCTA client:load />
        <PhoneLink phone={phone.tel} display={phone.display} variant="secondary" />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
